@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy & Data Transparency";
}

<div class="container mt-4">
    <div class="glass-panel p-4 p-md-5 mx-auto" style="max-width: 800px;">
        <h1 class="h3 fw-bold text-white mb-3"><i class="bi bi-shield-check text-info me-2"></i>Privacy Policy & Meteorological Data Ethics</h1>
        <p class="text-secondary mb-4">
            Atmosphere 360 is built with privacy-first architectural principles in accordance with educational and open data standards.
        </p>

        <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3 text-secondary">
            <div>
                <strong class="text-white d-block mb-1"><i class="bi bi-database me-1 text-primary"></i> Local Data Persistence</strong>
                All saved cities, search history, personal notes, and to-do lists are stored directly on your local machine using an embedded SQLite database (<code>weatherapp.db</code>). No personal data is sent to external advertising or profiling servers.
            </div>

            <div>
                <strong class="text-white d-block mb-1"><i class="bi bi-cloud-arrow-down me-1 text-info"></i> Open Weather Data APIs</strong>
                Live meteorological observations and forecasts are retrieved via secure HTTPS from Open-Meteo, an open-source weather forecasting service operating with high precision without tracking personal identifiers.
            </div>

            <div>
                <strong class="text-white d-block mb-1"><i class="bi bi-geo-alt me-1 text-danger"></i> Geolocation Privacy</strong>
                When you activate GPS Geolocation ("My Location"), your coordinates are evaluated client-side in the browser solely to query the local atmospheric station and are never stored without your explicit action.
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 pt-3 border-top border-secondary border-opacity-25">
            <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index" class="btn btn-modern-primary btn-sm">&larr; Return to Dashboard</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
